       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammssttrreettcchh--ggeenn is a program which uses ppaammssttrreettcchh(1) and ppaammssccaallee(1) to
       smoothly  scale  up a Netpbm image by any factor; it's like a more gen‐
       eral version of ppaammssttrreettcchh (hence the name).

       ppaammssttrreettcchh--ggeenn uses the --ddrrooppeeddggee option on ppaammssttrreettcchh.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       There are no command line options defined specifically for  ppaammssttrreettcchh--
       ggeenn, but it recognizes the options common to all programs based on lib‐
       netpbm (See
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ .)

       The Netpbm global options --qquuiieett and  --ppllaaiinn  did  not  exist  on  ppaamm‐‐
       ssttrreettcchh--ggeenn  prior  to version 10.86 (March 2019).  --qquuiieett did not work
       until version 10.91 (June 2020).



